## 🆕 Crear un Nuevo Módulo

### Paso 1: Crear Razor Class Library

```bash
dotnet new razorclasslib -n VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas -o VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas
cd VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas
```

### Paso 2: Configurar `.csproj`

```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="8.0.20" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\VRM_PluginDemo.Core.Abstractions\VRM_PluginDemo.Core.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
```

### Paso 3: Implementar `IModule`

```csharp
// FacturasModule.cs
using VRM_PluginDemo.Core.Abstractions;

namespace VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas;

public class FacturasModule : IModule
{
    public string ModuleId => "Facturas";
    public string DisplayName => "Gestión de Facturas";
    public string Description => "Módulo para gestión de facturas electrónicas";
    public string Version => "1.0.0";
    public string Author => "Equipo VRM";
    public string Category => "Finanzas";
    public List<string> Dependencies => new();
    public List<string> RequiredPermissions => new() { "Admin", "Finanzas" };

    public List<ModuleComponentInfo> GetComponents()
    {
        return new()
        {
            new ModuleComponentInfo
            {
                Name = "Facturas",
                Route = "/facturas",
                ComponentType = typeof(Components.Facturas),
                Icon = "bi-receipt",
                ShowInMenu = true,
                MenuOrder = 20
            }
        };
    }

    public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services, IConfiguration configuration)
    {
        services.AddScoped<IFacturaService, FacturaService>();
    }

    public async Task OnModuleLoadedAsync()
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"[{ModuleId}] Módulo cargado - v{Version}");
        await Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    public bool IsEnabledForClient(string clienteId) => true;
}
```

### Paso 4: Crear Componente Blazor

```razor
<!-- Components/Facturas.razor -->
@page "/facturas"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject IFacturaService FacturaService

<PageTitle>Gestión de Facturas</PageTitle>

<h1>💰 Gestión de Facturas</h1>

<!-- Tu UI aquí -->

@code {
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Lógica de inicialización
    }
}
```

### Paso 5: Crear `_Imports.razor` en `Components/`

```razor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode
@using VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas.Services

@namespace VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas.Components
```

### Paso 6: Compilar y Copiar

El módulo se copiará automáticamente a `Modules/` gracias al target en el `.csproj` del host:

```xml
<Target Name="CopyModulesToOutput" AfterTargets="Build">
  <ItemGroup>
    <ModuleFacturasFiles Include="..\VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas\bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\VRM_PluginDemo.Modules.Facturas.dll" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <Copy SourceFiles="@(ModuleFacturasFiles)" DestinationFolder="$(OutDir)Modules" />
</Target>
```

### Paso 7: ¡Listo!

Ejecuta la aplicación y el módulo se cargará automáticamente:

```bash
dotnet run --project VRM_PluginDemo.Blazor.Server
```

